course: dictionary
lesson: 1349
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Canal is one of these words. Look at the words around it, the context, before you decide.
explain: «A barge is a long flat boat on a canal» tells you that a canal is a long, narrow waterway that people dug so boats can travel. The boat and the water are the clues.
explain: «Swimmer's ear is an infection of the ear canal» uses canal in a different way. Ear and infection tell you that a canal here is a narrow tube inside your body. Always ask which meaning fits, then swap it into the sentence to check.
fact: A canal is a long, narrow waterway dug by people so boats can travel or water can flow.
fact: A canal can also be a narrow tube in the body, such as the ear canal.
fact: The ear canal is the tube that leads into your ear.
fact: Canal water is often deep and cold with steep sides, so never play near the edge.
fact: Famous canals include the Panama Canal and the Suez Canal, which carried goods by boat.
exercise: «A barge is a long flat boat on a canal.» What is a canal in this sentence? | A narrow tube inside the ear | A large hole in the ground | A sort of tall tower | *A long, narrow waterway dug so boats can travel
exercise: «Swimmer's ear is an infection of the ear canal.» What does canal mean here? | A waterway for boats | A rope pulled by a horse | *A narrow tube in the body | A type of boat
exercise: Ruby says the ear canal is a boat on the water. Is she right? | *No, it is a narrow tube in the ear | Yes, it is a long flat boat | No, it is a bridge over a river | Yes, it is a path beside the water
test: «The Suez Canal was dug largely by Egyptian workers.» What does canal mean in this sentence? | A rope for pulling boats | A type of bird | A narrow tube in the body | *A long, narrow waterway dug by people
test: Tom says, «Stay back from the edge, the water is deep and cold.» What should you learn from this? | Canals are only for fish | Boats must always stop at the edge | Canals are warm and shallow, so you can paddle | *Canal water can be dangerous, so keep away from the edge
exam: Which sentence uses canal to mean a narrow tube in the body? | Most goods cross the sea on giant ships | Ice on canals is very dangerous | *Swimmer's ear is an infection of the ear canal | A barge is a long flat boat on a canal
